<title>FRANCE: Aerospatiale complaint about Matra/BAe missile deal.</title>
<headline>Aerospatiale complaint about Matra/BAe missile deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned Aerospatiale has lodged a complaint against Lagardere subsidiary Matra Defense, claiming Matra breached a cooperation agreement by forming a missiles partnership with British Aerospace.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Aerospatiale said the complaint had been filed in September, and a public hearing was expected at the Tribunal de Commerce de Paris in late January.</p>
<p>Officials at Lagardere were not available for comment.</p>
<p>The Aerospatiale spokeswoman alleged that Matra had breached an accord to jointly produce Apache missiles by allying itself with British missiles interests and contributing an improved version of the missile, called the Storm Shadow.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
